  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "The bug was that `add_tag` used a list as its default for `tags`. Python creates that list once, so every call that left out `tags` added to the same list and tags from one call showed up in the next.\n\nI changed the default to `tags=None` and create a new empty list when it's `None`. If the caller passes their own `tags` list, the function still appends to that list directly. `remove_tag` is unchanged, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` passes (1/1).\n\nDONE: Fixed the shared default list in `add_tag` by using `tags=None` and creating a fresh list per call; `test_public.py` passes.",
